# rocknix_abl kit provenance

abl_signed-SM8750.elf is NOT committed here — the PKGBUILD fetches it from the
official ROCKNIX ABL release, pinned by tag + sha512:

  release:  https://github.com/ROCKNIX/abl/releases/tag/v1.1.7
  asset:    rocknix-abl-v1.1.7.tar.gz
  tarball sha512: fa1d213bec97661942b8083be1f2eb6b65cc200b4f3f76dd84261ba92a01ac92
                  61ed6834350f2f647a5ed82fcabadf5011b9ba6769f471abeaf06210ae9221c1
  abl_signed-SM8750.elf sha256 (release's own sidecar, re-checked in prepare()):
                  79e822791bcf088f72ef90601da02bfb8e8b268bf0489965f0213e95de45c311

It is ROCKNIX's patched, test-key-signed build of the Qualcomm ABL (edk2
LinuxLoader, BSD-3-Clause) for the SM8750 family — the bootloader that scans
for the FAT labeled ROCKNIX and boots /KERNEL (an Android boot image, board
dtb selected by board id). One elf serves every SM8750 board (AYN Odin 3,
KONKR Pocket FIT Elite); ROCKNIX keys the artifact by SoC.

The four kit files (README, flash_abl.sh.template, backup_abl.sh,
restore_backup_abl.sh) are VERBATIM copies from the ROCKNIX distribution repo,
packages/tools/rocknix-abl/sources/ (GPL-2.0 tree), as pinned by our `make
sync` snapshot. The PKGBUILD's %DEVICE% -> SM8750 substitution in
flash_abl.sh reproduces their package.mk. Vendored (4 tiny files, change
rarely) rather than fetched or synced; diff them against the ROCKNIX tree
when advancing the sync pin.

Version coupling: the ABL version ROCKNIX pins for the SoC lives in their
packages/tools/rocknix-abl/package.mk (PKG_VERSION). Ours (_ablver in the
PKGBUILD) should track it — the ABL defines the boot contract the sm8750
profile assumes (FAT label, /KERNEL boot image, board-id dtb select), so a
mismatched pair is the thing to avoid. v1.1.7 = their pin AND the latest
release as of 2026-08-11 (v1.1.7 adds USB boot and a standalone USB-only menu,
gates Internal boot mode to internal installs, drops the external boot mode and
the nuke-cfw option, and extends RawFat to the EFI boot path — the qcom-abl
boot contract is unchanged; kit scripts unchanged, diffed against their tree at
this bump).

The kit's job is FIRST INSTALL from stock Android: the user copies
rocknix_abl/ off the SD's boot FAT to Android internal storage, runs
backup_abl.sh (saves the stock abl_a/abl_b next to the scripts — tell users
to copy those .img backups OFF the device; an install-to-internal later
wipes userdata and the backup with it), then flash_abl.sh, both as root.
restore_backup_abl.sh is the road back to a fully stock device.

Once a device runs pocknix, ABL UPDATES no longer need Android: pocknix-update-abl
(pocknix-bsp-common, reachable from Pocknix Tools) flashes this same elf onto
abl_a/abl_b from the running system. It is user-run only — no alpm hook, nothing
at boot or update time, unlike ROCKNIX's updateabl which their bootloader
update.sh calls on every OS update. Its backup goes to /flash/rocknix_abl with
the kit's own filenames and is never overwritten, so a stock backup made the
Android way survives and restore_backup_abl.sh keeps working.

# openabl kit (SM8750)

abl_signed-SM8750.elf is NOT committed here — the PKGBUILD fetches it from the
OpenABL v1.2 release, pinned by tag + sha512:

  release:  https://github.com/OpenHandheldCollective/OpenABL/releases/tag/v1.2
  asset:    openabl-v1.2.tar.gz (one folder per chipset)
  tarball sha512: 41f8b0460bc5c2cbbec312911377e52c41eda7c4dcd365bc76486d81cf4da0e9
                  072df00edaf3afacb87565d856487d0aac3c8b5506d46b9ea6c901c319635492
  tarball layout used: openabl-v1.2/SM8750/abl_signed-SM8750.elf (+ .sha256 sidecar)
  SM8750/abl_signed-SM8750.elf sha256 (release's own sidecar, re-checked in prepare()):
                  0dba7b90d1a36e13977c00fec87f4f5ccc8f49b98864ad495a1ed04d35e33c3a

OpenABL boots Boot Loader Spec entries (loader/entries/*.conf, /Image, /dtbs)
written by pocknix-bls-deploy, NOT the Android /KERNEL the ROCKNIX ABL reads.
It is GPL-3.0 (corresponding source on the same release).

The four kit scripts are the same dd wrappers as the rocknix_abl kit, with
%DEVICE% -> SM8750 and /sdcard/rocknix_abl -> /sdcard/openabl (the folder the
user copies to Android internal storage). The ROCKNIX kit's copies are left
byte-identical to what it shipped.

Nothing flashes it automatically. The in-OS path is pocknix-update-abl, which
prefers openabl/ and falls back to rocknix_abl/ only when openabl/ is absent.

## 2026-11-10 — ROCKNIX kit bumped 1.1.8 -> 1.2 (assets, not behaviour)

ROCKNIX **deleted the assets** of the v1.1.8 release (the tag still exists, the
tarball 404s), so a clean rebuild of this package could not fetch the ELF it
shipped. Their current release, **v1.2** (2026-10-01), does publish
`rocknix-abl-v1.2.tar.gz` with `abl_signed-SM8750.elf` + `.sha256` sidecar, and
the qcom-abl boot contract is unchanged (FAT label, `/KERNEL` Android boot
image), so the fallback kit now comes from there.

- tarball sha512 `b2d897b4f681f22d416201e332a5c27efc00b0139c3b0806126f8913182285e803b8a3726a7c9a1609956049d4b6d054b3529bd0f508d1a86ab9ab3bf79dca01`
- `abl_signed-SM8750.elf` sha256 `48441f738a598feca19f30d009d3fc67c52776d5a1b58ff0fdfc331af15798a0`
  (1.1.8's was `bedff34b99bd06202301e78ee5ee025b81d5144c9773de179b5f48ba3b38455a` — the
  binaries differ, same size 258.048 B)

**The exact 1.1.8 we actually run is preserved**, byte for byte, as whole-slot
images: `abl_a.img` / `abl_b.img` (sha256 `8d7fd55d349620824a260b5b611a95aab81c1b8d8897856dbf09acaa4ad715da`,
1 MiB each, first 258.048 B = the 1.1.8 ELF, rest zeroes). They live on the
device in `/home/deck/abl-rollback-20261110/`, on `/flash/openabl/` after the
first `pocknix-update-abl` run, and off-device in the laptop's
`~/odin-backups/`. A revert is a `dd` of those images, not a package install.
